! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F202G sub-tests 11-18
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.45, octal 012036.40-012064.00) --
! the KR (Compare for Range) tests, run on the model. KR is the FP
! comparison whose result is GATED by the accumulator-high indicator
! (AH): "When AH is on, a comparison is performed ... and AE is set to
! one if the accumulator operand is low. If AH is off, the comparison
! is performed but the comparison indicators are not changed. AL is not
! changed" (Reference Manual p.91). AH is the input gate, never a
! result.
!
! Each pair of sub-tests exercises both gate states over one operand
! pair:
!   G11 AH ON : BB1,$AH sets AH=1; KR FK32,FK34; expect AH still ON
!   G12 AH OFF: Z,$IND clears AH;  KR FK32,FK34; expect AH still OFF
!   G13 AH ON : KR FPK1,FPK1 (equal); expect AH ON
!   G14 AH OFF: KR FPK1,FPK1; expect AE OFF (indicators left cleared)
!   G15 AH ON : KR FK40,FK25; expect AE ON (FK40 negative < FK25 positive)
!   G16 AH OFF: KR FK40,FK25; expect AL OFF
! FPK23 (pool p.176, octal 22034) reads "230" or "250" in the scan --
! 3 and 5 are near-identical in that typewriter font.  It is "250",
! settled by F205B, whose B20/B22 add FPK4 to the magnitude of FPK23
! and expect the all-ones FPK22: only "250" gives that, and the model
! on the "230" reading came out one unit short and halted.  This
! program carried "230" until 2026-09-07; its KR compares pass either
! way, which is why it went unnoticed.
!
!   G17 AH ON : KR FK34,FPK23; expect AH ON
!   G18 AH OFF: KR FK34,FPK23; expect AE OFF
! `BB1,$AH,$+1.` forces AH=1 (its target is the very next instruction,
! so control continues either way -- the branch is only for the set-bit
! side effect). Both that (indicator-bit set) and `Z,$IND` (indicator
! clear) are the capabilities added earlier this session (63721f1,
! b1a6ad0). A correct KR reaches the PASS halt substituted where the
! routine's SSIP exit begins; a wrong indicator branches to the SERS
! FAIL halt.
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, real listed addresses): SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch, PASS (octal 12064.40,
! the routine's `B,$+1.`/`B,F202G`/`B,SSW` exit) -> halt. Constants from
! the pools p.176-178 at their listed addresses.
!
! This block motivated a KR range-compare fix: fpCompare's range path
! used to set AH := (acc >= operand), but per p.91 KR leaves AL and AH
! unchanged and sets only AE (accumulator low). The fix removes the AH
! write. NOTE on discrimination: F202G's own operands do NOT distinguish
! that AH aspect -- all its AH-preset sub-tests (G11/G13/G17) have
! cmp >= 0 (e.g. G11's FK32 is positive, FK34 negative, so FK32 > FK34),
! so both the old (AH := cmp>=0 = 1) and the fixed (AH left = 1) code
! leave AH on and pass. The fix is kept because it is what p.91 says;
! it would matter for a future AH-preset/cmp<0/BZAH case. What F202G
! DOES discriminate is KR's AE result (see below).
! verify_fp_compare_g_listing.py checks every half-word and constant
! bit-for-bit against the printed machine code.
!
! Observed: the model halts at PASS -- KR gated by AH behaves as p.91
! specifies across all eight sub-tests. Discriminating injection (KR's
! AE forced off in the range path): halts at SERS at G15, which expects
! AE ON (FK40 negative < FK25 positive), exactly as predicted. Reversed
! by the exact inverse edit (AGENTS.md rule 2).

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pools, p.176-178) --
        SLC, (8)22006.0
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)22034.0
FPK23   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000525252525252525250
        SLC, (8)22173.0
FK25    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577777777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22202.0
FK32    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0027125252525252525000
        SLC, (8)22204.0
FK34    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0200377777777777777770
        SLC, (8)22212.0
FK40    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777577777777777777770

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)12036.40
F202G11 BB1, $AH, $+1.      ! force AH = 1
        L(U), FK32
        KR(U), FK34
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS          ! error if AH off
F202G12 L(U), FK32
        Z, $IND             ! AH = 0
        KR(U), FK34
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS           ! error if AH on
F202G13 BB1, $AH, $+1.
        L(U), FPK1
        KR(U), FPK1
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS
F202G14 L(U), FPK1
        Z, $IND
        KR(U), FPK1
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS           ! error if AE on
F202G15 BB1, $AH, $+1.
        L(U), FK40
        KR(U), FK25
        SIC, SEN
        BZAE, SERS          ! error if AE off
F202G16 L(U), FK40
        Z, $IND
        KR(U), FK25
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS           ! error if AL on
F202G17 BB1, $AH, $+1.
        L(U), FK34
        KR(U), FPK23
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS
F202G18 L(U), FK34
        Z, $IND
        KR(U), FPK23
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS

! -- PASS halt where the routine's SSIP exit begins --
        SLC, (8)12064.40
PASS    BEW, $

        END, F202G11
